  :adr/mirrors-precedent-gov-sec-edgar "structure is a byte-for-byte mirror of etzhayyim/org.worldbank.api: same 3-line .gitattributes (annex.backend=MD5E, .git* excluded, annex.largefiles=((mimeencoding=binary)and(largerthan=0))), same datalad create -c text2git convention (text stays plain git, only binaries would annex), same raw/source-catalog.edn shape. Standalone plain-git repo, deliberately NOT registered in manifest/repos.edn or west.yml, matching the org.worldbank.api / cloud-itonami-isic-* convention."
  :adr/verified-no-prior-art-gov-sec-edgar "owner explicitly asked whether isic-8291 or existing code already did this before building anything; a dedicated Explore agent confirmed no raw SEC EDGAR/XBRL archival exists anywhere in the superproject -- isic-8291 does on-demand lookup only (no archival), cloud-murakumo-market-intel's feed.cljc docstring explicitly states fetch-* fns 'never return a raw HTTP response', discarding it after parsing into summary facts."
  :adr/data-scope-gov-sec-edgar "28/28 companies -- the exact CIK set already present in cloud-murakumo-market-intel's data/company-facts.edn -- fetched live from data.sec.gov/api/xbrl/companyfacts/CIK{cik}.json, all HTTP 200, stored unmodified (no parsing/summarization) under raw/companyfacts/CIK<10-digit>.json. All 28 SHA-256 hashes in raw/source-catalog.edn independently recomputed from the actual files, not fabricated. Full 8000+ SEC filer universe explicitly deferred as a follow-up."
  :adr/b2-special-remote-not-established-gov-sec-edgar "HONEST LIMITATION: scripts/datalad-b2-init.cljs failed -- the only B2 bucket in manifest/repos.edn (gftdcojp-m365-annex) is already claimed by m365-archive's special remote (different annex UUID); the bucket-scoped key resolved via env/1Password/keychain cannot create a new bucket, and the account-level 1Password Master key needed for that was unresolvable non-interactively (op read hung). Deliberately did NOT work around this via --sameas (would entangle this unrelated public archive's metadata with a separate sensitive dataset's annex history). datalad push --to b2 fails with 'Unknown push target'. Materially harmless: text2git already commits all JSON as plain git blobs, and org.worldbank.api itself -- the precedent this repo mirrors -- was independently confirmed to also have NO live B2 special remote configured; GitHub push is the only persistence path either repo actually has. Establishing a real B2 remote (new bucket + account-level key) is an explicit follow-up, not silently assumed done."
